<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Solve Linear Equations: Mini-Lesson Review</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00036</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Solve Linear Equations: Mini-Lesson Review</md:title>
    <md:uuid>6d111ccb-e03b-4ccd-af91-25d122397ca4</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title><span>Solving Linear Equations Using a General Strategy</span></title>
<div data-type="note" id="fs-id1167835311076">
  <para>
    <para class="" id="fs-id1167834377117">A solution of an equation is a value of a variable that makes a true statement when substituted into the equation. For example, in \( x + 2 = 3 \), the value of the variable \( x \) is 1.</para>
    <para class="" id="fs-id1167834377117">To find the solution to an equation in one variable, the goal is to isolate the variable on one side of the equation. For example,</para>
    <para>\( 3x + 1 = 9 - x \)</para>
    <para>\( +x             +x \)</para>
    <para>\( 4x + 1 = 9 \)</para>
    <para>      \( -1    -1 \)</para>
    <para>      \( 4x = 8 \)</para>
    <newline/><para>You can check the solution by substituting the value into the equation.</para>
    <newline/><para>
      <para>\( 3(2) + 1 = 9 - 2 \)</para>
      <para>     \( 6 + 1 = 7 \)</para>
      <para>           \( 7 = 7 \)</para>
      <newline/><para>Equations may take several steps to solve, so it is helpful to have a clear and organized strategy. The following table shows a general strategy to solve any <emphasis>linear equation</emphasis> in one variable. You may not need to use every step.</para>
      <newline/><note>
        <!--BEGIN STEPS-->
        <title>General Strategy for Solving Linear Equations</title>
        <para><emphasis>Step 1 </emphasis>
          Simplify each side of the equation as much as possible.
          Use the <emphasis>Distributive Property</emphasis> to remove any parentheses.
          Combine like <emphasis>terms</emphasis>.
          <emphasis>Step 2 </emphasis>
          Collect all the variable terms on one side of the equation.
          Use the <emphasis>Addition or Subtraction Property of Equality</emphasis>.
          <emphasis>Step 3 </emphasis>
          Collect all the constant terms on the other side of the equation.
          Use the Addition or Subtraction Property of Equality.
          <emphasis>Step 4</emphasis>
          Make the <emphasis>coefficient</emphasis> of the variable term to equal to 1.
          State the solution to the equation.
          <emphasis>Step 5</emphasis>
          Check the solution. 
          Substitute the solution into the original equation to make sure the result is a true statement.
        </para>
        <!-- END STEPS -->
      </note>
    </para>
  </para>
</div>

<title><span data-type="" id="19">Try It: Solving a Linear Equation Using a General Strategy</span></title>
<para>Solve the following using a general strategy: </para>
<para>Solve \( 2(3x - 8) = 19 - x \).</para>
<para>Write down your answer, and then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </problem><solution>
  <title><span data-type="">Solution</span></title>
  <para>Here is how to solve this linear equation, \( 2(3x - 8) = 19 - x \), using a general strategy:</para>
  <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
    <thead/>
    <tbody>
      <row>
        <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">Distribute.</entry>
        <entry>\( 2(3x - 8) = 19 - x \)</entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">Add \( x \) to get the variables on the left.</entry>
        <entry>\( 6x + x - 16 = 19 - x + x \)</entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">Simplify.</entry>
        <entry>\( 7x - 16 = 19 \)</entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">Add 2 to get the constants on the right.</entry>
        <entry>\( 7x - 16 + 16 = 19 + 16 \)</entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">Simplify.</entry>
        <entry>\( 7x = 35 \)</entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">Simplify.</entry>
        <entry>\( 7x = 35 \)</entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">Divide by 7 to make the coefficient of the variable equal to 1.</entry>
        <entry>\( \frac{7x}{7} = \frac{35}{7} \)</entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">Simplify.</entry>
        <entry> \( x = 5 \)</entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">Check.</entry>
        <entry> \( 2(3x - 8) = 19 - x \)</entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">Substitute 5 for \( x \).</entry>
        <entry> \( 2(3(5) - 8) = 19 - (5) \)</entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">Simplify.</entry>
        <entry> \( 2(15 - 8) = 14 \)</entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">Simplify.</entry>
        <entry> \( 2(7) = 14 \)</entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">Simplify.</entry>
        <entry> \( 14 = 14 \) True \(\checkmark\)</entry>
      </row>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  
</solution></exercise>
</example><title>Check Your Understanding</title>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="4d5abc25-0828-4645-ac8e-8d56805a230e" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <exercise data-content-id="bcbf3602-7944-41bc-8a75-3e5b36561481" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-solution="\( n = 2 \)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\( n = - \\frac{4}{7} \\)&quot;, &quot;\\( n = -2 \\)&quot;, &quot;\\( n = 2 \\)&quot;, &quot;\\( n = -3 \\frac{5}{7} \\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Solve: \( 7(n - 3) - 8 = -15 \).</para>
    </problem>
    </exercise>
  <solution>
    <para>That’s correct! Check yourself: After using the Distributive Property and simplifying the left side, the expression is \( 7n - 29 \). To isolate the variable, add 29 to both sides and then divide both sides by 7.</para>
  </solution>
  </div>
